      "dcterms:title": "COLORED JONES POLYNOMIALS WITHOUT TAILS",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "LEE, CHRISTINE RUEY SHAN",
        "VEEN, ROLAND VAN DER"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20180612",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We exhibit an inﬁnite family of knots with the property that the ﬁrst coeﬃcient of the n-colored Jones polynomial grows linearly with n. This shows that the concept of stability and tail seen in the colored Jones polynomials of alternating knots does not generalize naively.",
